{"id":"mahabharata-9-025","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":25,"title":"पञ्चविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 25 · Bhima kills the elephants","summary":{"en":"After Bhima destroys the elephant force, he stabs the Kaurava ranks with his arrows, and in anger kills Duryodhana's charioteer. The Kaurava army, almost wholly slain, is left with a small remnant.","kn":"ಭೀಮ ಆನೆದಳವನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡಿ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಕೌರವ ಸಾಲುಗಳನ್ನು ಚುಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೋಪದಿಂದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಸಾರಥಿಯನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಬಹುತೇಕ ಹತವಾದ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಶೇಷವಾಗಿ ಉಳಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"भीम गज-सेना का नाश कर कौरव पंक्तियों को बाणों से बींधते हैं और क्रोध में दुर्योधन के सारथी को मार देते हैं। लगभग पूरी मारी जा चुकी कौरव सेना का छोटा-सा अंश रह जाता है।","te":"భీముడు గజసేనను నాశనం చేసి బాణాలతో కౌరవ వరుసలను గుచ్చుతాడు; కోపంతో దుర్యోధనుని సారథిని చంపుతాడు. దాదాపు పూర్తిగా హతమైన కౌరవసేన చిన్న అవశేషంగా మిగులుతుంది.","ta":"பீமன் யானைப்படையை அழித்துக் கௌரவ அணிகளை அம்புகளால் துளைத்து, சினத்துடன் துரியோதனனின் தேரோட்டியைக் கொல்கிறான். கிட்டத்தட்ட முற்றாக அழிந்த கௌரவப் படை சிறிதளவே எஞ்சுகிறது.","ml":"ആനപ്പടയെ നശിപ്പിച്ച ശേഷം ഭീമൻ തന്റെ അമ്പുകളാൽ കൗരവനിരകളെ കുത്തിമുറിക്കുന്നു; കോപത്തോടെ ദുര്യോധനന്റെ സാരഥിയെ കൊല്ലുന്നു. ഏതാണ്ട് പൂർണ്ണമായും കൊല്ലപ്പെട്ട കൗരവസേനയിൽ ചെറിയ ഒരു ശേഷിപ്പ് മാത്രം അവശേഷിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.25; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गजानीके हते तस्मिन्पाण्डुपुत्रेण भारत ।\nवध्यमाने बले चैव भीमसेनेन संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that elephant force had been destroyed by the son of Pandu, O Bharata, and the army was being cut down in battle by Bhimasena,"}},{"n":2,"text":"चरन्तं च तथा दृष्ट्वा भीमसेनमरिंदमम् ।\nदण्डहस्तं यथा क्रुद्धमन्तकं प्राणहारिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and seeing Bhimasena, the tamer of foes, moving about like angry Death, the life-taker, club in hand,"}},{"n":3,"text":"समेत्य समरे राजन्हतशेषाः सुतास्तव ।\nअदृश्यमाने कौरव्ये पुत्रे दुर्योधने तव ।\nसोदर्याः सहिता भूत्वा भीमसेनमुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"your remaining sons gathered in the battle, O king; with Duryodhana, the Kaurava, nowhere to be seen, the brothers united and rushed at Bhimasena."}},{"n":4,"text":"दुर्मर्षणो महाराज जैत्रो भूरिबलो रविः ।\nइत्येते सहिता भूत्वा तव पुत्राः समन्ततः ।\nभीमसेनमभिद्रुत्य रुरुधुः सर्वतोदिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Durmarshana, Jaitra, Bhuribala and Ravi: these sons of yours, united, charged at Bhimasena and hemmed him in on every side."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो भीमो महाराज स्वरथं पुनरास्थितः ।\nमुमोच निशितान्बाणान्पुत्राणां तव मर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, O great king, mounted his own chariot again and loosed sharp arrows at your sons' vital spots."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते कीर्यमाणा भीमेन पुत्रास्तव महारणे ।\nभीमसेनमपासेधन्प्रवणादिव कुञ्जरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showered by Bhima in that great battle, your sons held Bhimasena back, as men hold an elephant going downhill."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो रणे भीमः शिरो दुर्मर्षणस्य ह ।\nक्षुरप्रेण प्रमथ्याशु पातयामास भूतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, enraged in the battle, quickly cut off Durmarshana's head with a razor-headed arrow and felled it to the ground."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततोऽपरेण भल्लेन सर्वावरणभेदिना ।\nश्रुतान्तमवधीद्भीमस्तव पुत्रं महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with another broad-headed arrow that pierces all armor, the great chariot-fighter Bhima killed your son Shrutanta."}},{"n":9,"text":"जयत्सेनं ततो विद्ध्वा नाराचेन हसन्निव ।\nपातयामास कौरव्यं रथोपस्थादरिंदमः ।\nस पपात रथाद्राजन्भूमौ तूर्णं ममार च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as if laughing, he pierced Jayatsena with an iron arrow and threw that Kaurava from his chariot seat; he fell to the ground, O king, and died at once."}},{"n":10,"text":"श्रुतर्वा तु ततो भीमं क्रुद्धो विव्याध मारिष ।\nशतेन गृध्रवाजानां शराणां नतपर्वणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shrutarva, enraged, pierced Bhima, O revered one, with a hundred straight-jointed arrows feathered with vulture plumes."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो रणे भीमो जैत्रं भूरिबलं रविम् ।\nत्रीनेतांस्त्रिभिरानर्छद्विषाग्निप्रतिमैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, enraged in the battle, struck these three, Jaitra, Bhuribala and Ravi, with three arrows like poison and fire."}},{"n":12,"text":"ते हता न्यपतन्भूमौ स्यन्दनेभ्यो महारथाः ।\nवसन्ते पुष्पशबला निकृत्ता इव किंशुकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slain, those great chariot-fighters fell to the ground from their chariots, like kimshuka trees mottled with blossoms cut down in spring."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततोऽपरेण तीक्ष्णेन नाराचेन परंतपः ।\nदुर्विमोचनमाहत्य प्रेषयामास मृत्यवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with another sharp iron arrow, the scorcher of foes struck Durvimochana and sent him to death."}},{"n":14,"text":"स हतः प्रापतद्भूमौ स्वरथाद्रथिनां वरः ।\nगिरेस्तु कूटजो भग्नो मारुतेनेव पादपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killed, that best of chariot-fighters fell from his chariot to the ground, like a tree growing on a mountain peak broken by the wind."}},{"n":15,"text":"दुष्प्रधर्षं ततश्चैव सुजातं च सुतौ तव ।\nएकैकं न्यवधीत्संख्ये द्वाभ्यां द्वाभ्यां चमूमुखे ।\nतौ शिलीमुखविद्धाङ्गौ पेततू रथसत्तमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he killed your two sons Dushpradharsha and Sujata, one by one, each with two arrows at the front of the army; with their bodies pierced by arrows, those two best of chariot-fighters fell."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो यतन्तमपरमभिवीक्ष्य सुतं तव ।\nभल्लेन युधि विव्याध भीमो दुर्विषहं रणे ।\nस पपात हतो वाहात्पश्यतां सर्वधन्विनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then seeing another of your sons striving, Bhima pierced Durvishaha in the battle with a broad-headed arrow; he was killed and fell from his mount while all the archers looked on."}},{"n":17,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु निहतान्भ्रातॄन्बहूनेकेन संयुगे ।\nअमर्षवशमापन्नः श्रुतर्वा भीममभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his many brothers killed by one man in the battle, Shrutarva, in the grip of fury, advanced at Bhima."}},{"n":18,"text":"विक्षिपन्सुमहच्चापं कार्तस्वरविभूषितम् ।\nविसृजन्सायकांश्चैव विषाग्निप्रतिमान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He flung about a huge bow adorned with gold and let fly many arrows like poison and fire."}},{"n":19,"text":"स तु राजन्धनुश्छित्त्वा पाण्डवस्य महामृधे ।\nअथैनं छिन्नधन्वानं विंशत्या समवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that great battle, O king, he cut the Pandava's bow and then covered the bowless Bhima with twenty arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततोऽन्यद्धनुरादाय भीमसेनो महारथः ।\nअवाकिरत्तव सुतं तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great chariot-fighter Bhimasena, taking up another bow, covered your son with arrows and said, \"Stand! Stand!\""}},{"n":21,"text":"महदासीत्तयोर्युद्धं चित्ररूपं भयानकम् ।\nयादृशं समरे पूर्वं जम्भवासवयोरभूत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great was their battle, strange and fearsome, such as once took place between Jambha and Vasava."}},{"n":22,"text":"तयोस्तत्र शरैर्मुक्तैर्यमदण्डनिभैः शुभैः ।\nसमाच्छन्ना धरा सर्वा खं च सर्वा दिशस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole earth, the sky and all the directions were covered with the fine arrows they shot, like staffs of Yama."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः श्रुतर्वा संक्रुद्धो धनुरायम्य सायकैः ।\nभीमसेनं रणे राजन्बाह्वोरुरसि चार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shrutarva, enraged, drew his bow and struck Bhimasena in the arms and chest with arrows in the battle, O king."}},{"n":24,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो महाराज तव पुत्रेण धन्विना ।\nभीमः संचुक्षुभे क्रुद्धः पर्वणीव महोदधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply pierced by your son the archer, O great king, Bhima, angry, was stirred like the great ocean at the full moon."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततो भीमो रुषाविष्टः पुत्रस्य तव मारिष ।\nसारथिं चतुरश्चाश्वान्बाणैर्निन्ये यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, filled with fury, sent your son's charioteer and four horses to the house of Yama with arrows."}},{"n":26,"text":"विरथं तं समालक्ष्य विशिखैर्लोमवाहिभिः ।\nअवाकिरदमेयात्मा दर्शयन्पाणिलाघवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him chariotless, the immeasurable Bhima covered him with feathered arrows, showing the lightness of his hand."}},{"n":27,"text":"श्रुतर्वा विरथो राजन्नाददे खड्गचर्मणी ।\nअथास्याददतः खड्गं शतचन्द्रं च भानुमत् ।\nक्षुरप्रेण शिरः कायात्पातयामास पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shrutarva, chariotless, O king, took up sword and shield; as he took up his bright hundred-moon sword, the Pandava felled his head from his body with a razor-headed arrow."}},{"n":28,"text":"छिन्नोत्तमाङ्गस्य ततः क्षुरप्रेण महात्मनः ।\nपपात कायः स रथाद्वसुधामनुनादयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the great man's head cut off by the razor-headed arrow, his body fell from the chariot, making the earth resound."}},{"n":29,"text":"तस्मिन्निपतिते वीरे तावका भयमोहिताः ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्त संग्रामे भीमसेनं युयुत्सवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that hero fell, your men, bewildered with fear, charged at Bhimasena in the battle, eager to fight."}},{"n":30,"text":"तानापतत एवाशु हतशेषाद्बलार्णवात् ।\nदंशितः प्रतिजग्राह भीमसेनः प्रतापवान् ।\nते तु तं वै समासाद्य परिवव्रुः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they rushed on from the ocean of the army, now reduced to a remnant, the mighty armored Bhimasena met them; and they, reaching him, surrounded him on every side."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततस्तु संवृतो भीमस्तावकैर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nपीडयामास तान्सर्वान्सहस्राक्ष इवासुरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by your men, Bhima tormented them all with sharp arrows, as the thousand-eyed Indra does the asuras."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततः पञ्चशतान्हत्वा सवरूथान्महारथान् ।\nजघान कुञ्जरानीकं पुनः सप्तशतं युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he killed five hundred great chariot-fighters with their chariot-covers, and in the battle he killed seven hundred more of the elephant force."}},{"n":33,"text":"हत्वा दश सहस्राणि पत्तीनां परमेषुभिः ।\nवाजिनां च शतान्यष्टौ पाण्डवः स्म विराजते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed ten thousand foot soldiers and eight hundred horses with his excellent arrows, the Pandava shone."}},{"n":34,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु कौन्तेयो हत्वा युद्धे सुतांस्तव ।\nमेने कृतार्थमात्मानं सफलं जन्म च प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, Kunti's son, having killed your sons in the battle, thought himself to have fulfilled his purpose and his birth to be fruitful, O lord."}},{"n":35,"text":"तं तथा युध्यमानं च विनिघ्नन्तं च तावकान् ।\nईक्षितुं नोत्सहन्ते स्म तव सैन्यानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your armies, O Bharata, could not bear to look at him as he fought like that and cut down your men."}},{"n":36,"text":"विद्राव्य तु कुरून्सर्वांस्तांश्च हत्वा पदानुगान् ।\nदोर्भ्यां शब्दं ततश्चक्रे त्रासयानो महाद्विपान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having routed all the Kurus and killed their followers on foot, he made a noise with his arms, terrifying the great elephants."}},{"n":37,"text":"हतभूयिष्ठयोधा तु तव सेना विशां पते ।\nकिंचिच्छेषा महाराज कृपणा समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your army, O lord of the people, with most of its warriors killed, was left with only a few, O great king, and was in a pitiable state."}}]}]}